# Implementation Plan: MediSense RAG & Safety Evaluation Framework

Build the complete Evaluation Framework in `com.medisense.evaluation` featuring a 100-case benchmark (`eval_set.yaml`), distributed Redis locking, rate-limited sequential test execution, 9 precision evaluation metrics, persistence via Flyway V5 schema, and Admin REST API endpoints.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Evaluation Framework Architecture & Governance**:
> - **100-Case Benchmark Benchmark (`eval_set.yaml`)**:
>   - 20 Lab Explanation queries (en)
>   - 20 Prescription Explanation queries (en)
>   - 15 Health Claim Verification queries (en)
>   - 20 Adversarial Lab queries (en)
>   - 15 Adversarial Prescription queries (en)
>   - 10 Adversarial Claim queries (en)
>   - 10 Tamil Lab Explanation queries (ta)
>   - 5 Tanglish queries
>   - 5 Emergency Detection queries
> - **Concurrency & Rate Limits**: Max 1 concurrent run enforced via Redis distributed lock (`eval:lock:running`). Max 3 runs per hour per admin key (`X-Admin-Api-Key`). Bucket4j rate limiter within evaluation: 30 LLM calls per minute with a 500ms delay between cases.
> - **9 Precision Metrics**:
>   1. `citation_accuracy` (Target: ≥ 0.95)
>   2. `refusal_correctness_lab` (Target: 1.00)
>   3. `refusal_correctness_prescription` (Target: 1.00)
>   4. `hallucination_rate` (Target: ≤ 0.02)
>   5. `tamil_parity` (Target: ≥ 0.90)
>   6. `drug_name_integrity` (Target: 1.00)
>   7. `numeric_integrity` (Target: 1.00)
>   8. `adversarial_robustness_lab` (Target: 1.00)
>   9. `adversarial_robustness_prescription` (Target: 1.00)
> - **Endpoints**:
>   - `POST /internal/eval/run`
>   - `GET /internal/eval/results/latest`
>   - `GET /internal/eval/results/history`
>   - `GET /internal/eval/results/{run_id}/failures`

